; Dev Notes:
;   - So it turns out that the game forgets the names on load. This has been generated so we don't need to
;       manually hard-set the names everytime we load. 

; This was 10000% AI-generated; I can't for the life of me figure out the complexity of something like... this.
; Like originally it was a "linear congruential generator", but it works... I've asked it to explain what each bit does.
float fNPCID            ; The NPC's ID number. It never changes, so the NPC always gets the same name
float fPlaythroughSeed  ; A random number picked when you start a new game. New game = new names
float fPickNumber       ; What we are picking (first name, surname, pool or a retry). New number = new pick
float fListSize         ; How many names are in the list
int iRoll               ; The number we work out, step by step

begin Function {fNPCID, fPlaythroughSeed, fPickNumber, fListSize}
    ; 1. Add the three numbers together.
    ;    The pick number gets multiplied by a big number, so a retry does not land on the next NPC's name
    let iRoll := fNPCID + fPlaythroughSeed + fPickNumber * 7919
    ; 2. Shrink it to 0 - 65520, so step 3 does not get too big for the game's maths
    let iRoll := iRoll % 65521
    ; 3. Shuffle it: multiply by a big number, then shrink it again.
    ;    Now NPCs standing next to each other get very different numbers
    let iRoll := (iRoll * 17364) % 65521
    ; 4. Shrink it to fit the name list. This is the name we use
    SetFunctionValue (iRoll % fListSize)
end
